      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jphacks/tkb_2615/git/trees/dd3b0f076772135fd113137f90a405d058b759df"
    },
    "message": "Check at the end of a tick only what can have changed (stage B2)\n\nTickEngine.step now calls WorldState.validate_after_tick. With the Rust kernels it\nkeeps a memo of the last passed check and skips what is provably unchanged: config\nchecks, settled support requests, unchanged presence, lifecycle and overlay states,\nthe newest shared operations record, and relationship records no dict watcher\nreported a write to. Large loops first ask a Rust check that accepts only what the\nPython rules accept; anything else goes to those rules, which alone raise errors.\n\nWithout the kernels every tick runs the plain per-tick validation. The full\nvalidation keeps its rules and results. Seven-day project route: per-tick validation\n70.9 s to 14.6 s (1.45 ms per tick), with the same world, events and KPI hashes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
